+
+# Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+Export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Supports `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`, applied in order.
+- Returns a new document; neither the document nor the patch is mutated, and added values are copied.
+- Throws when the patch is not an array, an operation is malformed (unknown `op`, missing or
+  non-string `path`/`from`, missing `value`), or an operation fails (unresolvable target, bad array
+  index, move into own child, failed `test`).
+- `test` compares deeply, regardless of object key order, with strict types.
+- Member names such as `__proto__` are plain data.
+
+## Outcome
+
+Implemented in `src/index.ts` (reusing the RFC 6901 pointer parsing), tested in `src/index.test.ts`
+(RFC 6902 appendix A examples, immutability and error cases); `npm test` passes.
